Data types:
1) Numbers: positive, negative, zero - int

2) Characters: A-Z, a-z, special characters - char

3) Real numbers: float, double

; - represents the end of the statement

Format Specifier: 
1) int - %d
2) char - %c
3) float - %f
4) double - %lf(long float)

No. of bytes:
1) int - 4 bytes - 32 bits
2) char - 1 byte - 8 bits
3) float - 4 bytes - 32 bits
4) double - 8 bytes - 64 bits
